within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.R_RespiratorySystem.R03D_OtherSystemicDrugsForObstructiveAirwayDiseases.R03DX05_Omalizumab;
model Omalizumab_Oh2023_PD_itch_severity_score
  "linear exposure-response sweep — Oh_2023 :: itch severity score (weekly itch severity score)"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Interfaces.PartialExposureResponseSweep(
    E0 = 13.5,      // [1]
    Emax = 0, EC50 = 1,      // unused by a line
    exposure_per_s = 1);
  parameter Real slope = 0.0172   "[1]";
equation
  response = E0 + slope*exposure;
  // family_inferred: the record's model family is effect_compartment; read from the parameters: a slope and no Emax — linear
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 1000, Interval = 2),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>Omalizumab_Oh2023_PD_itch_severity_score</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Oh E et al., <i>CPT: pharmacometrics &amp; systems pharmacology 12(6):795–807</i> 2023 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1002/psp4.12953\">doi:10.1002/psp4.12953</a>) — weekly itch severity score against total omalizumab — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: linear.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    =       13.5          drug-free response (baseline) (Baseline itch severity score, Q324)
  slope =     0.0172          change in response per unit of exposure (Slope term in linear drug effect model, Q335)</pre><p>The algebra is <code>response = E0 + slope*exposure</code>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one  of total omalizumab per second of simulated time: there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 13.5   (drug-free)</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Oh_2023: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"));
end Omalizumab_Oh2023_PD_itch_severity_score;
